  * Wait for reboot

==== Terminal Upgrade Process ====

If you don't have a GUI (LuCI) available, you can alternatively upgrade via the command line.

  * Login as root via SSH on 192.168.1.1, then enter the following commands:

<code>
cd /tmp
wget http://downloads.openwrt.org/snapshots/trunk/XXX/xxx.abc
sysupgrade /tmp/xxx.abc
</code>
=====Migrating to 24.10.x=====

The OEM layout on the Edgerouter X has two kernel slots that are 3MB each. Starting with [[https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/commit/2967e24d02775f63d9e363e6e0d351716dcc3f7c | Linux 6.6 commit 2967e24]] the kernel images no longer fit into this layout. This means a special migration is required to adjust the partition layout and upgrade successfully to 24.10.x releases (include current RC images). Attempting to use normal `sysupgrade` will provide an error advising to use this migration process. Updating without following the migration instructions will break the device. 

The scripts in this [[https://github.com/darkxst/erx-migration|repository]] can be used to migrate existing installs 21.02, 22.03 or 23.05 to the new layout. It will install the latest 24.10 release candidate to your device.

====Upgrade Process====
**WARNING** All settings will be wiped make sure to backup your settings before proceeding.

1. If you are still on Stock OS install factory images for [[https://github.com/stman/OpenWRT-19.07.2-factory-tar-file-for-Ubiquiti-EdgeRouter-x|22.03]] first

2. Login to router using ssh

3. Copy both scripts from [[https://github.com/darkxst/erx-migration|Edgerouter-X migration scripts]] to the "/tmp" folder on your router:
  *  	 ubnt_erx_migrate.sh
  *  	 ubnt_erx_stage2.sh
4. Run below shell commands

<code>
cd /tmp
./ubnt_erx_migrate.sh
</code>


5. This will download firmware update, check sha256 sums, then flash new kernel and rootfs and finally reboot.

Further details and documentation can be found here:

  * [[https://github.com/darkxst/erx-migration#migration|Github repository with Edgerouter-X migration scripts]]

